{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nThe Files preview shows `.md` files as syntax-highlighted raw text. When browsing a README or docs, the rendered form — the same one the GitHub view already uses for issue / PR bodies — is much easier to read.\n\n## Spec\n\n- Files whose extension is `.md` / `.markdown` (extension-only detection; extensionless files like `README` are out of scope) are rendered with the GitHub view's markdown renderer. Move `markdown_to_lines` out of `github::panes::detail_view::view` into a shared `core::ui::markdown` module.\n- The layout follows the preview pane width and reflows on resize (tables use the existing width-fitting logic).\n- `m` toggles rendered / raw (the current highlighted text); the preview header shows `markdown` / `raw`.\n- Config: a top-level `markdown-preview \"render\" | \"raw\"` node picks the default (default `render`), mirroring `image-preview`. `m` is a session-local toggle.\n- Scrolling, search (`/`) and `o` / `O` (open in external app) behave as for raw text; search matches the rendered text.\n- The existing text-preview size cap (truncated display) applies unchanged. Front matter (`---` blocks) is shown as-is in a dim style.\n- Relative images (`![](assets/x.png)`) are not drawn — link text only, as the renderer already does.\n\n## Docs / demo\n\n- README / README.ja Files key tables; guide Files chapter and Config Reference (`markdown-preview`, CI-verified kdl example).\n- `tape/demo-files.tape`: select a `.md`, toggle with `m`; re-record the GIF.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-03T04:50:10Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":154,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Files: render Markdown files in the preview pane"}
